Chapter: BvtPlayCoin
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UoaixPlays stage 5: a play's give and take of coin move it between the cast member's purse and the player's; a short
 purse gives what it holds, and an empty one moves nothing. A payment pays the economy's transfer tax, so the payer loses
 the amount and the payee gains what cg-play-coin returns, at most the amount.
  bvt-play-coin : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-play-coin (unused) = when cg-new 0
    is Err (e) -> bvt-check ("play coin fixture: " & e) False
    is Ok (owner) -> let x = owner.vendor.currency
      in let cast = cg-label-actor x (cg-cast-owner + 1)
      in let player = cg-label-actor x 3002
      in let town = eu-open x 4 1
      in let granted = eu-grant x True 1 town 200 0 0
      in let funded = if cast < 1 then -1 else eu-pay x True town (ep-actor x.world cast).purse 50 0 0
      in let purse = if cast < 1 then 0 else (ep-actor x.world cast).purse
      in let wallet = if player < 1 then 0 else (ep-actor x.world player).purse
      in let cast0 = (em-purse x.copper purse).coin
      in let player0 = (em-purse x.copper wallet).coin
      in let given = cg-play-coin owner cast player 1 30 0 True
      in let cast1 = (em-purse x.copper purse).coin
      in let player1 = (em-purse x.copper wallet).coin
      in let short = cg-play-coin owner cast player 1 1000 0 True
      in let cast2 = (em-purse x.copper purse).coin
      in let player2 = (em-purse x.copper wallet).coin
      in let empty = cg-play-coin owner cast player 1 5 0 True
      in let player3 = (em-purse x.copper wallet).coin
      in let taken = cg-play-coin owner player cast 1 10 0 False
      in let cast4 = (em-purse x.copper purse).coin
      in let player4 = (em-purse x.copper wallet).coin in act
      print-line-uni ("PLAYCOIN funded=" & show cast0 & " given=" & show given & " short=" & show short & " empty=" & show empty & " taken=" & show taken & " wallet=" & show player4)
      a <- bvt-check "give copper takes 30 from the cast member's purse and the player gains what it returns; take moves 10 back the same way" (cast > 0 & player > 0 & funded >= 0 & cast0 > 30 & given > 0 & given <= 30 & cast1 == cast0 - 30 & player1 == player0 + given & taken > 0 & taken <= 10 & player4 == player3 - 10 & cast4 == cast2 + taken)
      b <- bvt-check "a short give hands over all the purse holds; an empty purse gives nothing and moves nothing" (short > 0 & short <= cast1 & cast2 == 0 & player2 == player1 + short & empty < 0 & player3 == player2)
      a + b
    end
